    "explanation": "<p class=\"text-sm leading-6 text-muted-foreground\">Non-communicable diseases (NCDs) are long-lasting health conditions that do not spread from person to person. They progress slowly and often require long-term management. Examples include cardiovascular disease, Type 2 diabetes, and liver disease.</p>",
